  "reviews": [
    {
      "author": "Gordon",
      "content": "This movie would make a GREAT survival horror game.\r\n\r\nThe movie itself was really good, it had solid acting and it didn't seem to rely on jump scares. The story was good and fleshed out and the things they didn't reveal, they explained in good time.\r\nNot too gory and was a great balance of horror and story telling.\r\n\r\nI would recommend this movie to anyone who likes story driven horror films.",
      "rating": 8,
      "createdAt": "2026-03-29T03:14:37Z"
    },
    {
      "author": "Sierbahnn",
      "content": "This is not Ghost Ship\r\nI think this movie wanted to be Ghost Ship, or at least as good as Ghost Ship. It didn't reach there. The characters were engaging enough and the direction solid, but the look of the movie wasn't grand, and the monster just looked floaty and unrealistic, given how it was rendered into the scenes. It just wasn't believable, had no agenda, and no reason. It was just a \"scary thing\" skulking about.",
      "rating": 5,
      "createdAt": "2026-05-05T10:55:34Z"
    },
    {
      "author": "GregLikesMovies",
      "content": "Cinematography, editing, acting, special effects, production design, all of it good. Its just too bad the script is at times embarrassingly juvenile; with cringeworthy dialog and wafer thin characters who act without rhyme or reason. A bad movie wrapped in a pretty package. Not recommended for those of average wit or above.",
      "rating": 3,
      "createdAt": "2026-07-16T11:45:45Z"
    }
  ],
